  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Turning an action into a topic or object",
     "texto": [
      "**-는 것** lets you talk about an action as «doing…» or «the act of…»: 수영하다 → **수영하는 것** (swimming), 여행하다 → **여행하는 것** (travelling), 요리하다 → **요리하는 것** (cooking). When a particle follows, **것** is often contracted: **수영하는 걸 좋아해요** is the spoken form of **수영하는 것을 좋아해요**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Talking about likes",
     "texto": [
      "With **좋아하다/싫어하다**, the nominalised action usually takes the object particle **을/를**: **여행하는 것을 좋아해요** (I like travelling), **수영하는 것을 싫어해요** (I don't like swimming). With **좋다/싫다**, it is common to mark it as the topic with **은/는**: **수영하는 것은 싫어요**. These constructions are related, but the particles and predicate are not simply interchangeable."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
